  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Crumble the ground beef into a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook and stir until almost brown. Add onions, celery and garlic and cook until meat is no longer pink and onion is tender.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain grease, and transfer beef, onions and garlic to a slow cooker. Add taco seasoning (or chili powder to meat) and stir to coat meat.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix in the tomato soup (undiluted), potatoes, carrots and beans.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Cover, and cook on the Low setting for 4 to 5 hours, until stew is thick and potatoes are tender.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Season to taste with salt, pepper and.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I cooked it for about 6 hours...everything was done perfect. Served it with hot cornbread...a definite keeper recipe!"
    },
    {
      "text": "Can also cook in a dutch oven at 325 degrees for 1 hour then reduce the temperature to 200 degrees for 4 more hours. Yummy on a cool autumn night!"
    },
    {
      "text": "Recipe can be easily doubled. Try 1 can kidney beans and 1 can black beans for visual appeal."
    }
  ],
